id: pm-rlm-release-gate
title: Release readiness behind PM_RELEASE_APPROVED
description: "Prepare daily OIDC publishing behind one repository approval variable. Verify metadata, allowlisted packed files, privacy, regression checks, npm and Bun release gates. The owner performs the first npm publish and trusted-publisher setup; keep approval unset."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:23:47.260Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T00:16:18.849Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:23:51.749Z",codex-agent,"Normalize daily scheduling and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED job gates while preserving release decisions, generated changelogs and release notes. Verify OIDC publishing without a stored npm token, manifest metadata, packed allowlists and private-data scans. No open homepage/author PR was found during orientation. No publishing, trust setup, approval variable changes or merges are authorized."
  "2026-10-26T01:03:12.232Z",codex-agent,"Opening the release-readiness PR after package allowlist/privacy verification and focused regression proofs so complete npm and Bun CI can run in parallel with local full-gate verification. Pending checks are explicitly not treated as passing evidence. No timeout, threshold, dependency pin or test case is being relaxed."
  "2026-10-26T01:11:29.339Z",codex-agent,"Pack verification: npm pack --dry-run --json and the actual npm pack --ignore-scripts artifact agree on 103 allowlisted files (dist: 76; docs: 17; examples: 1; root files: 9). Every packed member was scanned for absolute home paths, npm/GitHub/cloud tokens, private keys, hosted-data locations, private addresses and historical owner email addresses: PASS with zero matches. Regression proof: five independent workflow mutations (approval, provenance, token environment, daily schedule and OR bypass) plus the original manifest each fail the new contract check; restored contract passes 4/4. The linked test also passes through pm test --run --progress. Next gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check with isolated HOME and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-26T02:24:47.669Z",codex-agent,"Required complete npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASS in isolated GitHub CI at 5ef4a35ea0ca1027c8a06086090a02e0b163ea26. Main suite counts: npm 266/266, Bun 266/266; every required matrix job succeeded. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40252329410. The shared-host npm attempt timed out inside a shallow-revert child fixture, despite 100 percent measured coverage. Duplicate local work was stopped after complete isolated CI passed. No failed or interrupted local attempt is counted as a pass. No timeout, case, threshold or dependency pin was changed. Packed artifact allowlist/privacy checks and linked regressions passed. Final tracker evidence is being committed and CI will recheck that final head. Keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T00:14:57.096Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: preserve existing release-readiness work and merged main changes. Remove automatic release-workflow enablement; the orchestrator enables disabled schedules after merge. Require the canonical repository at job level for every write-permission or publishing job in the affected workflows, alongside the existing approval and branch conditions. Prove guard, approval, provenance and token regressions independently, then wait for complete npm and Bun CI on the pushed head."
  "2026-10-27T00:16:07.257Z",codex-agent,"Packed-artifact verification: 113 allowlisted files; dry-run and actual archive agree, and every packed member has zero private-data findings. Local project health passes with extensions disabled; globally installed extension version skew is outside this package."
  "2026-10-27T00:16:13.420Z",codex-agent,"Fork-exclusion revert proof: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-approval.test.ts passes 6/6. Independently reverting each job repository guard, reverting all repository guards, allowing an OR bypass, removing approval or provenance, injecting a synthetic npm token environment, adding an unguarded CI write job, inheriting CI write permissions, adding a read-permission CI publisher, and restoring automatic setup all fail (each command exits nonzero; 12 independent mutations rejected). Restoring the workflows passes 6/6. Linked pm tests, test typecheck where present and lint pass. Canonical-repository checks include inherited permissions. Disabled release workflows remain for the orchestrator to enable after merge; no live settings or publishing were changed."
